Falsifies `kernel::syscall::proofs::the_run_end_is_exact_and_refuses_exactly_what_does_not_fit`.

The defect is milestone 142's MAJOR 4 restored: `run_end_va` computes the last page of
a run as `va + (count - 1) * PAGE_SIZE` and checks only the **addition**. The multiply
wraps, so a `count` large enough to bring `(count - 1) * 4096` back around to a small
number yields a `last_va` sitting a few pages above `va`, and both mapping paths
(`page_frame_map` and `MAP_INTO`) then admit a run that spans the address space having
checked two addresses that are neighbours.

`wrapping_sub` and `wrapping_mul` rather than plain `-` and `*` on purpose: Kani reports
an arithmetic overflow as a failure of its own, and a harness that goes red because the
solver found a panic proves nothing about the property. This makes the code wrong in
exactly the way the real defect was wrong, and leaves the harness the only thing that can
object.

Expected to fail: `assert!(last as u128 == want, "the last page of the run is va + (count
- 1) * PAGE_SIZE, with no wrap")`. Confirmed red on 2026-09-01.

The sibling harness `every_page_between_the_checked_ends_is_itself_a_user_page` stays
green under this patch, which is the honest half of the record: it reasons about a run
whose two ends are already given, so it never calls this function.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@
 /// fit in a `u64`, or `count` is zero. The multiply is checked as well as the add. Both mapping
 /// paths guard on it, and `syscall::proofs` proves it exact.
 pub(super) fn run_end_va(va: u64, count: u64) -> Option<u64> {
-    va.checked_add(count.checked_sub(1)?.checked_mul(paging::PAGE_SIZE)?)
+    va.checked_add(count.wrapping_sub(1).wrapping_mul(paging::PAGE_SIZE))
 }
 
 /// Undo the first `mapped` pages of a failed run-map in the space rooted at `root`: unmap each
